# GitHub workflow

Use **issues + branches + PRs** for feature and bugfix work. Roadmap stays in [`docs/BACKLOG.md`](docs/BACKLOG.md); full process in [`docs/WORKFLOW.md`](docs/WORKFLOW.md). Branch model: [integration-branch.mdc](integration-branch.mdc).

## Starting work

1. **Issue** — one issue per backlog item; use repo templates (Feature / Bugfix).
2. **Branch** from **`integration`**: `feature/<issue#>-kebab-slug` or `fix/<issue#>-kebab-slug`.
3. **BACKLOG** — `[~]` in **In progress** with `Issue: #N`.

## Cursor Cloud

- Prefer CLI: `./scripts/cloud-agent.sh <issue#>` (reads issue via `gh`, no URL pasting). See [`docs/WORKFLOW.md`](docs/WORKFLOW.md#start-an-agent-from-the-cli-recommended).
- Agent works only on that branch; does not mix other backlog items.
- Deliverable: **PR into `integration`** with `Closes #<issue>`, BACKLOG updated, `./scripts/build.sh` passes.
- **May merge into `integration`** when CI build is green and scope is a single issue — **except** face/UI PRs (see integration-branch.mdc).
- **Do not merge to `main`** (use promotion script).

## Finishing

1. Face / input changes: **Integration device gate** or `./scripts/functional_test.py --flash` on `integration` before promotion.
2. Visual polish: optional [hardware-qa.mdc](hardware-qa.mdc) screenshot on an issue.
3. PR description uses [`.github/pull_request_template.md`](../.github/pull_request_template.md).
4. Backlog **Done** line includes date + PR link.
5. **`main`**: only via `./scripts/promote-integration.sh --flash-ok` after device gate + flash QA.

## Do not

- Implement multiple unrelated backlog items on one branch.
- Push or merge to **`main`** (use promotion script).
- Commit secrets.
- Rely on compile-only CI as proof of face correctness.
